    {
      "s": "Bloomberg Tech",
      "t": "Netherlands to Fight Rollout of Proposed US Curbs on ASML",
      "d": "The Dutch government said it will resist US plans to further restrict ASML Holding NV’s sales to China, calling the proposed rules a threat to Europe’s most valuable company and widening a rift with Washington.",
      "u": "https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2026-11-26/netherlands-plans-to-fight-rollout-of-proposed-us-curbs-on-asml",
      "m": "11. 26. PM 12:23",
      "ts": 1795695792000,
      "fullText": "Technology Netherlands to Fight Rollout of Proposed US Curbs on ASML Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift Gift this article Contact us: Provide news feedback or report an error Confidential tip? Send a tip to our reporters Site feedback: Take our Survey New Window Facebook X LinkedIn Email Link Gift By Patrick Van Oosterom and Sarah Jacob November 26, 2026 at 12:23 PM UTC Updated on November 26, 2026 at 4:54 PM UTC Bookmark Save Takeaways by Bloomberg AI The Dutch government said it will resist US plans to further restrict ASML Holding NV ’s sales to China, calling the proposed rules a threat to Europe’s most valuable company and widening a rift with Washington. The US’s Match Act, which aims to stymie China’s progress in the chip industry, would force the Netherlands and other allies to strengthen export controls on advanced equipment, including Veldhoven, Netherlands-based ASML’s chipmaking machines. The Dutch government is opposed to the extraterritorial scope of the bill, trade minister Sjoerd Sjoerdsma said in parliament on Thursday."
